---
import CompareLayout from '../../layouts/CompareLayout.astro'

const comparison = [
  { aspect: 'What it analyzes', figma: 'Figma files only', buoy: 'Your actual shipped code' },
  { aspect: 'Source of truth', figma: 'Figma designs', buoy: 'Codebase implementation' },
  { aspect: 'Catches AI drift', figma: 'No', buoy: 'Yes, the primary use case' },
  { aspect: 'Runtime values', figma: 'Not visible', buoy: 'Full visibility' },
  { aspect: 'Coverage scope', figma: 'Design files', buoy: 'All code files' },
  { aspect: 'CI/CD integration', figma: 'Limited', buoy: 'Full GitHub App' },
  { aspect: 'Cost', figma: 'Varies by plugin', buoy: 'Free CLI' },
]
---

<CompareLayout
  title="Buoy vs Figma Plugins | Code-First Design Drift Detection"
  description="Figma plugins only see Figma. Buoy scans your actual shipped codebase for design drift."
  keywords="figma plugin alternative, code design comparison, figma to code"
  heroTitle="Figma Plugins vs Code Analysis"
  heroDescription="Figma plugins analyze your design files. Buoy analyzes your actual code. The code is what ships."
  competitor="Figma Plugins"
>
  <div slot="hero" class="ui-tray"><div class="ui-panel">
    <div class="ui-panel-head">Same button, two places</div>
    <dl class="hf-rows hf-rows--flush">
      <div><dt>Figma file</dt><dd>Fill: <span class="ui-token">color/primary</span></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Button.tsx</dt><dd>color: <span class="ui-old">#3b82f6</span> <span class="hf-them">(written by an AI assistant)</span></dd></div>
    </dl>
    <dl class="hf-rows">
      <div><dt>Figma plugin</dt><dd class="hf-them">Sees what you designed. Looks fine.</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="ui-c-buoy">Buoy</dt><dd>Sees what you shipped: <span class="ui-old">#3b82f6</span> should be <span class="ui-token">var(--color-primary)</span></dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div></div>

  <section class="ui-section">
    <div class="ui-wrap">
      <div class="ui-head">
        <h2>Feature comparison</h2>
        <p>Figma plugins analyze <span class="ui-c-warn">what you designed</span>. Buoy analyzes <span class="ui-c-buoy">what you shipped</span>. They're often different, especially with AI-generated code.</p>
      </div>
      <table class="ui-table cmp-table mt-10">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Aspect</th><th scope="col">Figma plugins</th><th scope="col" class="cmp-buoy">Buoy</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {comparison.map((row) => (
            <tr><th scope="row">{row.aspect}</th><td class="cmp-them">{row.figma}</td><td class="cmp-buoy">{row.buoy}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ui-section ui-section--band">
    <div class="ui-wrap">
      <div class="ui-head"><h2>The problem with Figma-only analysis</h2></div>
      <ol class="ui-steps">
        <li><span class="ui-step-n">1</span><div><h3>AI doesn't look at Figma</h3><p>When developers use Copilot or Claude to write code, the AI doesn't have access to your Figma files. It generates code that works but doesn't follow your design system. Figma plugins can't catch this: they only see Figma.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="ui-step-n">2</span><div><h3>Code drifts from design</h3><p>Even without AI, code drifts from design over time. Quick fixes, edge cases, "temporary" solutions. Figma shows what was designed. Buoy shows what was actually built.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="ui-step-n">3</span><div><h3>Runtime values matter</h3><p>Some values are computed at runtime, come from APIs, or are set in CSS-in-JS. Figma plugins can't see these. Buoy scans the actual code that runs.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ui-section">
    <div class="ui-wrap">
      <div class="ui-head">
        <h2>Buoy + Figma integration</h2>
        <p>Buoy can connect to your Figma files to compare design tokens and components. Get the best of both: Figma as source of truth, Buoy for code verification.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6"><a href="/integrations/figma" class="ui-link">Learn about the Figma integration</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</CompareLayout>

<style is:global>
  .hf-code { margin: 0; padding: 18px 20px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.7; background: var(--color-term); color: var(--color-body); }
  .hf-rows--flush { border-top: 0 !important; background: var(--color-term); }
  .hf-rows { margin: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line); }
  .hf-rows > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 96px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 12px; padding: 13px 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .hf-rows > div:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .hf-rows dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-ink); }
  .hf-rows dd { margin: 0; color: var(--color-ink); }
  .hf-rows .hf-them { color: var(--color-muted); }
</style>
